CM_ "BLR-v1 brake-lamp relay board -> anyone listening, bus 0, IDs 0x620-0x62F (device class 2).
NOT stock Honda messages. The board lights the brake lamps from openpilot's own 0x1FA BRAKE_LIGHTS
bit, which the car ignores, and reports what it is doing here.

COPIED, NOT WRITTEN. Every message, signal, comment and value table below is the firmware's own
blr/dbc/blr.dbc (board repo S:/Software/EPS-LKAS, branch blr-v1, read at e8854f9), cut verbatim for the
telemetry frames 0x620-0x624, 0x627 and 0x62F (0x623/0x624 are sent by the bench image only since
frame layout 2). Change the firmware's file first and copy it again;
test_blr.py decodes the firmware's golden frames (fixtures/blr_golden_frames.json) through this file
and fails on any difference. The boot channel 0x628-0x62A is not copied: it only exists offroad,
during an update, when nothing is logging.

Intel byte order (@1+) throughout, LSB first, unlike most Honda frames. No signal is named COUNTER
or CHECKSUM: in a honda_ DBC those names make the parser demand a Honda checksum the board does
not compute, and every frame would be dropped. BLR_SEQ is the board's loss detector.

Registered liveness-exempt (float nan) in carstate.py: the board can be absent, sitting in its
bootloader, or have its transmitter off for the power cycle, and none of that may ever cost
openpilot its CAN.

DIAGNOSTICS ONLY. Nothing here feeds brakePressed, brakeLights, any controls decision or panda
safety. DRIVER_BRAKING and EXT_SINK are the board's own view of the brake-lamp circuit;
0x17C BRAKE_PRESSED and BRAKE_SWITCH stay the only brake-pedal input openpilot has.

FRAME LAYOUT 2 since 2026-11-01 (0x627 FRAME_LAYOUT, a 4-byte 0x620): every field openpilot decodes
kept its bit, so either layout decodes right here. Routes recorded before it carry layout 1 (an
8-byte 0x620), whose other bits this file misreads: read those with the firmware's
blr/tools/blr_layout1.dbc.";

BO_ 1568 BLR_STATUS: 4 BLR
